# Runbook fix D2 (2026-10-21), R5 bind arm only, node B only: every MutationStage task that handles a MUTATION_REQ
# sleeps 2 s at the entry of MutationVerbHandler.doVerb. The message is already deserialized there
# (InboundMessageHandler.java:427-429: provideMessage() before consumer.accept), so each RUNNING task holds its mutation
# for 2 s and B applies at most v/2 writes/s: the pool binds at every v <= 128 against 400/s (S) and 100/s (L).
RULE mps hold running mutation task
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.db.MutationVerbHandler
METHOD doVerb
AT ENTRY
IF true
DO Thread.sleep(2000L)
ENDRULE
